**1.** A method for detecting at least one target harmful substance in a consumable sample, the method comprising:

receiving a consumable sample within a microfluidic testing chamber;

contacting the consumable sample with a functionalized sensor substrate positioned within the microfluidic testing chamber, wherein the functionalized sensor substrate comprises a plurality of capture probes configured to selectively bind to the at least one target harmful substance;

generating a detectable signal upon binding of the at least one target harmful substance present in the consumable sample to the plurality of capture probes;

detecting, via a signal detector, a physical characteristic of the generated signal;

comparing, by a processor executing computer-readable instructions, the detected physical characteristic of the signal to a predetermined calibration baseline stored in a memory; and

determining, based on said comparing, at least one of the presence, absence, or concentration of the target harmful substance within the consumable sample.
